                  exemplar: "Individual and Group Work:\n• Learner(s) go through a Repertoire Selection Exercise, justify their choice, and sign a Contract to work on the piece in the semester off school-time-tabled schedules. However, see teachers in a one-on-one practical instruction session a week to evaluate and assess progress.\n\nCollaborative Learning:\n• Research and select a global issue and piece(s)\n• Learners prepare their pieces for the entire semester.\n• Assign roles (e.g., choreographer, composer, scriptwriter)\n• Learner(s) OR Group(s) work individually (self-study/self-taught/community experts support), and collaboratively with teachers, and colleagues' learners to develop skills and apply them in the selected repertoire as [DANCE, MUSIC or DRAMA, or a collaboration].\n• Plan for the presentation or the performance of the five to ten-minute repertoire of artistic products prepared.\n• Do group rehearsals of the selected repertoire and document your SWOT analysis for Class Presentation.\n\nExploratory Learning:\nExplore different artistic expressions [DANCE, MUSIC, and DRAMA] to convey a message about a global issue. Students work individually or in small groups to:\n• Investigate and research different artistic styles and techniques\n• Experiment with different forms of expression\n• Create and rehearse a 5-10 minute artistic product\n• Reflect on their process and final product",
